  "why": "Every entry declares a PostgreSQL `date` column as a TypeScript `Date`. TypeORM's PostgresDriver.prepareHydratedValue normalizes `date` to a 'YYYY-MM-DD' STRING before any transformer runs, so the declared type is an unchecked lie: `.toISOString()` / `.getFullYear()` compile and throw at runtime the moment a row exists (APA-130). Converting a site to `DateOnlyColumn()` from @aquaculture/backend-common/database removes it from this list.",
